          up: {"title":"Spot the spacing errors (Challenge)","intro":"<p>These lines from the Form 5 newsletter look tidy at first glance. Read each one character by character.</p>","q":"Tap EVERY line that contains at least one spacing error.","lines":["1. The meeting is at 10:30 am in Room 5 (Block B).","2. Bring your SBA folder ; it will be checked.","3. The principal said,\"Phones must be switched off.\"","4. Late-comers will not be admitted – no exceptions.","5. Results: 28 passed,2 were absent.","6. Ms. Lake's class won the quiz!","7. The fair runs from 9:00 am to 1 :00 pm.","8. Our motto is \" Excellence in all things \".","9. The well -known author (from Anguilla) will speak.","10. Is the hall booked? Please confirm by Friday."],"correct":[1,2,4,6,7,8],"win":"Well spotted. Line 2 has a space before the semicolon; line 3 has no space after the comma; line 5 has no space after the comma; line 7 has a space before the colon in the time; line 8 has spaces inside the quotation marks; line 9 has a space before the hyphen. Lines 1, 4, 6 and 10 are correct.","miss":"Look again. Some errors are a single character: a missing space after a comma, one space before a colon in a time, or one space beside a hyphen. Lines 1, 4, 6 and 10 are correct."}
