          up: {"title":"Did the typist apply the signs? (typed line) (Challenge)","intro":"<p><b>Manuscript:</b></p><p class=\"passage\">The <u>P</u>rize-giving <b>[/ lc]</b> ceremony <u>also will</u> <b>[tr]</b> be held in the ^<sup>main</sup> school hall on <u>Thurs.</u> <b>[sp]</b> 10 <u>d</u>ecember <b>[caps]</b>. <s>All</s> <b>[stet]</b> parents and <u>guar dians</u> <b>[close up]</b> are <u>warmlywelcome</u> <b>[#]</b>.</p><p>Below is the line the typist keyed in, word by word, exactly as typed.</p>","q":"Tap EVERY word in the typed line that is still wrong.","lines":["The","prize-giving","ceremony","will","also","be","held","in","the","main","school","hall","on","Thurs.","10","december.","All","parents","and","guar","dians","are","warmlywelcome."],"correct":[13,15,19,20,22],"win":"Well done. \"Thurs.\" should be \"Thursday\" (Sp), \"december\" needs a capital D (Caps), \"guar dians\" should be closed up to \"guardians\", and \"warmlywelcome\" needs a space (#). The lower-case p, the transposition, the insertion of \"main\" and the stet on \"All\" were all applied correctly.","miss":"Look again, sign by sign. Four signs were missed: Sp, Caps, close up and #. Remember that \"All\" is correct, because stet restores it."}
