        {
          type:'write', title:`Key in a marked-up notice`, genre:`Typescript from manuscript (manuscript signs and abbreviations)`,
          stimulus:`<p><b>Manuscript from Ms Small (Calabash Point Secondary):</b></p><p class="passage"><u>t</u>he <u>computerlab</u> <b>[caps] [#]</b> will be closed on <u>Wed.</u> <b>[sp]</b> for <u>main tenance</u> <b>[close up]</b>. Students <u>shd</u> save all their <u>info</u> to USB drives before the end of class on <u>Tues.</u> <b>[sp]</b> <b>[¶]</b> The new ^<sup>colour</sup> printers will be installed by the <s>the</s> <b>[delete]</b> IT <u>dept</u> and the lab will reopen <u>morning early</u> <b>[tr]</b> on <u>Thurs.</u> <b>[sp]</b><br><b>[run on]</b> <s>Please</s> <b>[stet]</b> report any problems to Ms Small <u>immed</u>.</p>`,
          prompt:`<p>Key in the notice as a correct typescript. Apply <b>every</b> manuscript sign and expand <b>every</b> abbreviation that should not remain abbreviated. Use blocked paragraphs.</p>`,
          min:45, max:120,
          frame:`<p>The computer lab will be closed on ... for maintenance. Students should ...</p><p>The new ... printers ...</p>`,
          checklist:[
            `I applied the caps, # and close up signs (The, computer lab, maintenance).`,
            `I spelt out Wed., Tues. and Thurs. and expanded shd, info, dept and immed.`,
            `I inserted "colour", deleted the repeated "the" and transposed "morning early".`,
            `I started a new paragraph at the ¶ sign and ran the last sentence on.`,
            `I kept "Please" because of the stet sign.`
          ],
          rubric:[
            {criterion:`Signs applied`, marks:5, look:[`^The computer lab|\\bThe computer lab\\b`, `maintenance`, `colour printers`, `early morning`, `by the IT`, `\\bPlease report`], min:4,
              strong:`You applied the manuscript signs accurately, including the stet, transposition and insertion.`,
              weak:`Apply each sign: capital T in "The", a space in "computer lab", close up "maintenance", insert "colour", delete the repeated "the", transpose to "early morning", and keep "Please" (stet).`},
            {criterion:`Expanded abbreviations`, marks:4, look:[`Wednesday`, `Tuesday`, `Thursday`, `should`, `information`, `department`, `immediately`], min:5,
              strong:`You expanded every abbreviation correctly.`,
              weak:`Type all shorthand in full: Wednesday, Tuesday, Thursday, should, information, department, immediately.`},
            {criterion:`Accuracy`, marks:3, look:[`^(?![\\s\\S]*\\b(shd|info|dept|immed)\\b)`, `^(?![\\s\\S]*\\b(Wed|Tues|Thurs)\\.)`, `^(?![\\s\\S]*the the)`], min:2,
              strong:`No shorthand or repeated words remain in your typescript.`,
              weak:`Proofread against the manuscript: no shorthand (shd, info, dept, immed), no abbreviated days, and no repeated "the the" should remain.`}
          ],
          model:`<p>The computer lab will be closed on Wednesday for maintenance. Students should save all their information to USB drives before the end of class on Tuesday.</p><p>The new colour printers will be installed by the IT department and the lab will reopen early morning on Thursday. Please report any problems to Ms Small immediately.</p>`,
          teacherTip:`<p>Before you type, go through the manuscript with a pencil and number every sign (there are 16 changes here, counting each abbreviation). After typing, tick each number off against your typescript. This is the fastest way to make sure nothing is missed under exam conditions.</p>`,
          easy: {"genre":"Typescript from manuscript: a short notice (7 marks)","stimulus":"<p><b>Shorter manuscript (Calabash Point Secondary):</b></p><p class=\"passage\"><u>t</u>he <u>computerlab</u> <b>[caps] [#]</b> will be closed on <u>Wed.</u> <b>[sp]</b> for maintenance. Students <u>shd</u> save their work ^<sup>today</sup>. <s>Please</s> <b>[stet]</b> ask the IT <u>dept</u> for help.</p><p><b>Sign key:</b> caps = capital letter; # = add a space; sp = spell in full; ^ = insert the word above; stet = keep the crossed-out word. Also type the shorthand <u>shd</u> and <u>dept</u> in full.</p>","prompt":"<p>Key in the notice as a correct typescript. There are <b>7 changes</b> to make. Tick them off as you go.</p>","min":20,"max":60,"frame":"<p>The computer lab will be closed on ... for maintenance. Students should ... Please ...</p>","checklist":["I typed a capital T and a space in \"computer lab\".","I typed Wednesday in full.","I typed should and department in full.","I inserted \"today\".","I kept \"Please\" because of the stet sign."],"rubric":[{"criterion":"Signs applied","marks":4,"look":["\\bThe computer lab","Wednesday","work today","Please ask"],"min":3,"strong":"You applied the signs correctly.","weak":"Apply each sign: The computer lab, Wednesday, insert \"today\", and keep \"Please\"."},{"criterion":"Shorthand expanded","marks":2,"look":["should","department"],"min":2,"strong":"Both pieces of shorthand are typed in full.","weak":"Type \"should\" and \"department\" in full."},{"criterion":"Accuracy","marks":1,"look":["^(?![\\s\\S]*\\b(shd|dept|Wed)\\b)"],"min":1,"strong":"No shorthand remains.","weak":"Check that shd, dept and Wed. no longer appear."}],"model":"<p>The computer lab will be closed on Wednesday for maintenance. Students should save their work today. Please ask the IT department for help.</p>","key":"<p>Mark scheme (7): signs 4 (The computer lab with both changes 1, Wednesday 1, today inserted 1, Please kept 1); shorthand 2 (1 each); accuracy 1 (no shorthand or abbreviated day left).</p>","teacherTip":"<p>The sign key and the stated number of changes are the scaffolds here. Ask Foundation students to number the seven changes on the manuscript first, then tick each one off after typing. Remove the sign key once they can do this, and move them to the Core notice with sixteen changes.</p>","title":"Key in a marked-up notice (Foundation)"},
          up: {"genre":"Typescript from manuscript with explanations (15 marks)","stimulus":"<p><b>Manuscript from the IT coordinator (Calabash Point Secondary):</b></p><p class=\"passage\"><u>computer lab closure</u> <b>[caps]</b><br><u>t</u>he <u>computerlab</u> <b>[caps] [#]</b> will be closed from <u>Wed.</u> <b>[sp]</b> 25 <u>Nov.</u> <b>[sp]</b> to <u>Fri.</u> <b>[sp]</b> 27 <u>Nov.</u> <b>[sp]</b> for <u>main tenance</u> <b>[close up]</b>. Students <u>shd</u> save all their <u>info</u> to the school cloud ^<sup>account</sup> before the end of class on <u>Tues.</u> <b>[sp]</b> 24 <u>Nov.</u> <b>[sp]</b> <b>[¶]</b> The new ^<sup>colour</sup> printers will be installed by the <s>the</s> <b>[delete]</b> IT <u>dept</u>, <s>and</s> <b>[stet]</b> the <u>L</u>ab <b>[/ lc]</b> will reopen <u>morning early</u> <b>[tr]</b> on <u>Mon.</u> <b>[sp]</b> 30 <u>Nov.</u> <b>[sp]</b><br><b>[run on]</b> Please report any problems, <u>e.g.</u> a printer that will not connect <u>w</u> your laptop, to Mr Brooks <u>immed</u>.</p>","prompt":"<p>Answer both parts.</p><ol type=\"a\"><li><b>Key in</b> the notice as a correct typescript, with the heading on its own line. Apply every manuscript sign, expand every abbreviation that should not remain, and use blocked paragraphs. <i>(12 marks)</i></li><li>In one sentence each, <b>explain</b> why you (i) kept the word \"and\", (ii) kept \"e.g.\", and (iii) typed \"Nov.\" in full. <i>(3 marks)</i></li></ol>","min":100,"max":220,"frame":"<p><b>(a)</b> COMPUTER LAB CLOSURE<br>The computer lab will be closed from Wednesday 25 November to ...<br>The new colour printers ...<br><b>(b)</b> (i) I kept \"and\" because ... (ii) I kept \"e.g.\" because ... (iii) I typed \"Nov.\" in full because ...</p>","checklist":["The heading is in capitals on its own line.","Every day and month is in full, and the dates are unchanged.","I inserted \"account\" and \"colour\", deleted the repeated \"the\", transposed \"morning early\" and lowered the L in \"Lab\".","I started a new paragraph at the ¶ and ran the last sentence on into paragraph 2.","I kept \"and\" (stet) and \"e.g.\" (accepted), and expanded shd, info, dept, w and immed."],"rubric":[{"criterion":"Signs applied","marks":6,"look":["COMPUTER LAB CLOSURE","\\bThe computer lab","maintenance","cloud account","colour printers","by the IT",", and the lab","early morning"],"min":6,"strong":"You applied the signs accurately, including the stet, transposition and both insertions.","weak":"Apply each sign: capitals in the heading, The computer lab, maintenance, insert account and colour, delete the repeated the, keep and (stet), lower-case lab, early morning."},{"criterion":"Abbreviations expanded","marks":4,"look":["Wednesday 25 November","Friday 27 November","Tuesday 24 November","Monday 30 November","should","information","department","immediately","with your laptop"],"min":7,"strong":"Every abbreviation that should be expanded has been typed in full.","weak":"Type every day and month in full, and expand shd, info, dept, w and immed."},{"criterion":"Accuracy and layout","marks":2,"look":["^(?![\\s\\S]*\\b(shd|info|dept|immed)\\b)","^(?![\\s\\S]*the the)","e\\.g\\."],"min":3,"strong":"No shorthand or repeated words remain, and e.g. has been kept.","weak":"Check that no shorthand or \"the the\" remains, and that the accepted \"e.g.\" is still there."},{"criterion":"Explanations","marks":3,"look":["stet|let it stand","accepted|may stay|allowed|standard abbreviation","formal|in full|days and months|month"],"min":3,"strong":"All three decisions are explained using the correct rule.","weak":"Explain: stet means let it stand; e.g. is an accepted abbreviation; months are typed in full in a formal document."}],"model":"<p><b>(a)</b></p><p>COMPUTER LAB CLOSURE</p><p>The computer lab will be closed from Wednesday 25 November to Friday 27 November for maintenance. Students should save all their information to the school cloud account before the end of class on Tuesday 24 November.</p><p>The new colour printers will be installed by the IT department, and the lab will reopen early morning on Monday 30 November. Please report any problems, e.g. a printer that will not connect with your laptop, to Mr Brooks immediately.</p><p><b>(b)</b> (i) I kept \"and\" because the stet sign means let it stand, so the crossing out is ignored. (ii) I kept \"e.g.\" because it is an accepted abbreviation that may stay in a finished document. (iii) I typed \"Nov.\" in full because the Sp sign asks for it and months are typed in full in a formal document.</p>","key":"<p>Mark scheme (15): (a) signs 6 (1 per two signs correctly applied, max 6), abbreviations 4 (deduct 1 per abbreviation left, minimum 0), accuracy and layout 2 (1 no new errors or repeated words, 1 heading and blocked paragraphs). (b) 1 per correct explanation.</p>","teacherTip":"<p>This Challenge manuscript has over 25 changes, including a stet, a run on and a lower-case sign that are easy to miss. Insist on a numbered pencil pass before typing. In (b), the student must name the rule, not just say \"because it was marked\"; that is what shows real understanding of the signs.</p>","title":"Key in a marked-up notice (Challenge)"}
        }
