          up: {"title":"Making the pharmacy notice mailable (Challenge)","intro":"<p>The manager of Bay Street Pharmacy wants 200 copies of a customer notice printed before opening. The notes include a quotation from the head pharmacist. Choose the BEST option each time.</p>","nodes":{"start":{"text":"<p>The notes have four paragraphs (two indented, two blocked) and a quotation. Which layout do you use?</p>","choices":[{"t":"Indented paragraphs throughout, with the quotation typed in capitals.","to":"ok1","fb":"The paragraphs are consistent, but capitals are not a way to show a quotation; an inset paragraph is."},{"t":"Copy the notes exactly, mixed styles and all.","to":"bad1","fb":"Mixed paragraph styles make the notice unmailable."},{"t":"Blocked paragraphs throughout, with the quotation as an inset paragraph.","to":"n2","fb":"Excellent. One consistent paragraph style, with the quotation set off from both margins."}]},"n2":{"text":"<p>The notes say: \"From Mon. 2 Nov. the pharmacy will open at eight am. 4 pharmacists &amp; twelve assistants are now on staff.\" Which version is mailable?</p>","choices":[{"t":"\"From Monday 2 November the pharmacy will open at 8:00 am. 4 pharmacists and 12 assistants are now on staff.\"","to":"bad2","fb":"A sentence must not begin with a numeral, and four is below ten anyway."},{"t":"\"From Monday 2 November the pharmacy will open at 8:00 am. Four pharmacists & 12 assistants are now on staff.\"","to":"bad2","fb":"The ampersand must be typed as \"and\" in running text."},{"t":"\"From Monday 2 November the pharmacy will open at 8:00 am. Four pharmacists and 12 assistants are now on staff.\"","to":"n3","fb":"Correct. Day and month in full, the time in numerals, \"Four\" spelt out at the start of the sentence, 12 in numerals and \"and\" for the ampersand."}]},"n3":{"text":"<p>The notes say: shorten the quotation, keeping \"Your health comes first\" and \"we are here to help\" and leaving out the words between. Which is correct?</p>","choices":[{"t":"\"Your health comes first, we are here to help.\"","to":"bad3","fb":"This hides the omission and changes the quotation. An ellipsis must show where words were left out."},{"t":"\"Your health comes first ... we are here to help.\"","to":"n4","fb":"Correct. Three full stops with a space before and after mark the omission."},{"t":"\"Your health comes first...we are here to help.\"","to":"ok2","fb":"The ellipsis is there, but house style needs a space before and after it."}]},"n4":{"text":"<p>The spelling check finds nothing. Which check is BEST before you print 200 copies?</p>","choices":[{"t":"Print all 200 copies; the checker found nothing.","to":"bad4","fb":"The checker cannot see real words used wrongly or missing words."},{"t":"Read it once quickly on screen.","to":"ok3","fb":"Better than nothing, but one quick pass misses real-word errors and wrong figures."},{"t":"Proofread against the notes, checking every figure and name character by character, then do a second pass for language and layout, and ask a colleague to read it.","to":"good","fb":"The strongest routine. Two passes plus a fresh pair of eyes catch what the checker cannot."}]},"good":{"text":"<p><b>Mailable!</b> Your colleague spots \"Open form 8:00 am\" in the footer, which the checker missed. You fix it, print 200 perfect copies, and the manager signs off. You used one paragraph style, an inset quotation, a correct ellipsis and every figure rule.</p>","end":"good"},"ok1":{"text":"<p><b>Nearly.</b> The paragraphs are consistent, but the quotation in capitals looks like shouting and is not a recognised layout. Try again.</p>","end":"ok"},"ok2":{"text":"<p><b>Nearly.</b> The omission is shown, but the ellipsis spacing does not follow house style. Small details decide mailability. Try again.</p>","end":"ok"},"ok3":{"text":"<p><b>Risky.</b> A single quick read misses \"form\" for \"from\" in the footer, and a customer points it out. Try again.</p>","end":"ok"},"bad1":{"text":"<p><b>Not mailable.</b> The manager points at the uneven paragraphs: \"Pick one style.\" Try again.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad2":{"text":"<p><b>Not mailable.</b> The figure rules were not fully applied. Every number must follow the rules. Try again.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad3":{"text":"<p><b>Misquoted.</b> The head pharmacist says she never said those words in that way. Show omissions honestly with an ellipsis. Try again.</p>","end":"bad"},"bad4":{"text":"<p><b>200 wasted copies.</b> Every notice on the counter says \"Open form 8:00 am\". Try again.</p>","end":"bad"}}}
